# no caller hands mark() a function, so nothing passes the test in front of its store and no run comes to it: the callee writes nothing. As the front end writes it
# function mark(o: unknown) { if (typeof o === "function") (o as any).seen = 1; }  mark(1); mark("text");
# f1 = mark
# TODO: unions-and-narrowing-4: the front end writes the store behind the test on the value from in front of it (PropSet v0, not the parameter of the block that the test proves), so the scan lays no test on its subject until listOf() answers with the name behind the test
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f1 {{*}}layouts-written=none
# RUN(NEVER): link functions mechanisms=all
# NEVER-NOT: function f1 {{*}}mayCallUnknownCode
# NEVER-NOT: function f1 {{*}}fields-written
